<!-- Original Curious Signals draft adaptation; GPL-3.0 for this implementation. Source lesson attribution and limits: docs/drafts/exomoon-photometry.md. -->
<phyphox version="1.17" locale="en">
  <title>Draft: Exomoon overlap photometry</title>
  <category>Curious Signals drafts</category>
  <description>Nano mode 6 direct photometry of a planet and moon analogue. Preserve RGBC counts with both clocks; compare manually entered planet-only, separated and overlapping means to distinguish added blocking from overlap brightening.</description>
  <data-containers>
    <container size="0">device_time</container>
    <container size="0">receive_time</container>
    <container size="0">clear</container>
    <container size="0">red</container>
    <container size="0">green</container>
    <container size="0">blue</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">enabled</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">dark</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">baseline</container>
    <container size="1">den</container>
    <container size="0">normalized</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">planet_mean</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">separate_mean</container>
    <container size="1" init="0">overlap_mean</container>
    <container size="1">extra_depth_candidate</container>
    <container size="1">extra_depth_gated</container>
    <container size="1">extra_depth</container>
    <container size="1">overlap_brightening_candidate</container>
    <container size="1">overlap_brightening_gated</container>
    <container size="1">overlap_brightening</container>
  </data-containers>
  <input>
    <bluetooth id="Sense" name="phyphox-sense" mode="notification" subscribeOnStart="true">
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian" offset="0">device_time</output>
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian" offset="4">clear</output>
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian" offset="8">red</output>
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian" offset="12">green</output>
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian" offset="16">blue</output>
      <output char="cddf1002-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" extra="time">receive_time</output>
    </bluetooth>
  </input>
  <output>
    <bluetooth id="Sense" name="phyphox-sense">
      <config char="cddf1003-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian">6</config>
    </bluetooth>
  </output>
  <analysis sleep="0.1">
    <formula formula="[1]-[2]">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">baseline</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">dark</input>
      <output clear="true">den</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="([1_]-[2])/([3]-[2])*((heaviside([3]-[2])*sign([3]-[2]))/(heaviside([3]-[2])*sign([3]-[2])))*((1-sign(abs([4]-1)))/(1-sign(abs([4]-1))))">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">clear</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">dark</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">baseline</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">enabled</input>
      <output clear="true">normalized</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="([1]-[2])/[3]">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">planet_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">separate_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">den</input>
      <output clear="true">extra_depth_candidate</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1]*((heaviside([2])*sign([2]))/(heaviside([2])*sign([2])))*((1-sign(abs([3]-1)))/(1-sign(abs([3]-1))))">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">extra_depth_candidate</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">den</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">enabled</input>
      <output clear="true">extra_depth_gated</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1]*((heaviside([2]-(0)))/(heaviside([2]-(0))))*((heaviside((1)-[3]))/(heaviside((1)-[3])))*((heaviside([7]-[4]))/(heaviside([7]-[4])))*((heaviside([4]-[6]))/(heaviside([4]-[6])))*((heaviside([6]-[5]))/(heaviside([6]-[5])))*((heaviside([5]-[8]))/(heaviside([5]-[8])))">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">extra_depth_gated</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">extra_depth_candidate</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">extra_depth_candidate</input>
      <output clear="true">extra_depth</output>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">planet_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">separate_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">baseline</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">dark</input>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="([1]-[2])/[3]">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">separate_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">den</input>
      <output clear="true">overlap_brightening_candidate</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1]*((heaviside([2])*sign([2]))/(heaviside([2])*sign([2])))*((1-sign(abs([3]-1)))/(1-sign(abs([3]-1))))">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_brightening_candidate</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">den</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">enabled</input>
      <output clear="true">overlap_brightening_gated</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1]*((heaviside([2]-(0)))/(heaviside([2]-(0))))*((heaviside((1)-[3]))/(heaviside((1)-[3])))*((heaviside([7]-[4]))/(heaviside([7]-[4])))*((heaviside([4]-[6]))/(heaviside([4]-[6])))*((heaviside([6]-[5]))/(heaviside([6]-[5])))*((heaviside([5]-[8]))/(heaviside([5]-[8])))">
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_brightening_gated</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_brightening_candidate</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_brightening_candidate</input>
      <output clear="true">overlap_brightening</output>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">planet_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">separate_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">overlap_mean</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">baseline</input>
      <input type="buffer" clear="false">dark</input>
    </formula>
  </analysis>
  <views>
    <view label="Acquisition">
      <graph label="Raw clear counts" labelX="Receive time" labelY="Clear counts" unitX="s" unitY="counts" partialUpdate="false" style="lines">
        <input axis="x">receive_time</input>
        <input axis="y">clear</input>
      </graph>
      <value label="Device time (separate clock)" unit="s" precision="4">
        <input>device_time</input>
      </value>
      <graph label="Normalized light curve" labelX="Receive time" labelY="Relative signal" unitX="s" unitY="1" partialUpdate="false" style="lines">
        <input axis="x">receive_time</input>
        <input axis="y">normalized</input>
      </graph>
    </view>
    <view label="Calibration">
      <edit label="Enable reduction (0 or 1)" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true" min="0" max="1">
        <output>enabled</output>
      </edit>
      <edit label="Dark/background mean" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true">
        <output>dark</output>
      </edit>
      <edit label="Unocculted baseline mean" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true">
        <output>baseline</output>
      </edit>
    </view>
    <view label="Characteristic means">
      <edit label="Planet-only plateau mean" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true">
        <output>planet_mean</output>
      </edit>
      <edit label="Planet and moon separated mean" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true">
        <output>separate_mean</output>
      </edit>
      <edit label="Planet and moon overlap mean" default="0" signed="true" decimal="true">
        <output>overlap_mean</output>
      </edit>
      <info>Select settled windows using the exported receive-time trace; calculate their means outside this app and enter them here in counts. Use identical geometry, baseline and background. Both bodies must be inside the disk in compared windows, with a matched planet silhouette. Extra depth=(planet-only-separated)/(baseline-dark); brightening=(overlap-separated)/(baseline-dark). No automatic event classification. Compare signatures with window scatter and motor-only controls; source proof pp.3-8.</info>
      <value label="Resolved extra depth" unit="1" precision="4">
        <input>extra_depth</input>
      </value>
      <value label="Overlap brightening" unit="1" precision="4">
        <input>overlap_brightening</input>
      </value>
    </view>
    <view label="Setup">
      <info>Mount globe, Nano and orbit rigidly; add a separately rotating moon. Film from detector viewpoint. Obtain planet-only and motor-only controls. Keep both silhouettes fully inside the disk in characteristic windows. Rods and motor shadows can mimic features. F=1-(Ap+Am-Apm)/As uses projected areas. No moon radius or TTV/TDV is inferred. Same moon phase each planetary orbit requires Tplanet/Tmoon integer; rational ratios repeat after multiple orbits.</info>
      <info>Draft software only. Import, BLE delivery, Android/iOS button behavior and physical apparatus remain to be validated. Counts are not lux. Keep source geometry and spectral output fixed; test linearity and avoid clipping. Changing current settings recalculates the live curve; export before changing runs. Device seconds and receive seconds are independent clocks. Do not infer timing precision from nominal firmware rate.</info>
    </view>
  </views>
  <export>
    <set name="Raw Nano mode 6">
      <data name="receive_time">receive_time</data>
      <data name="device_time">device_time</data>
      <data name="clear">clear</data>
      <data name="red">red</data>
      <data name="green">green</data>
      <data name="blue">blue</data>
    </set>
    <set name="Current controls">
      <data name="enabled">enabled</data>
      <data name="dark">dark</data>
      <data name="baseline">baseline</data>
      <data name="planet_mean">planet_mean</data>
      <data name="separate_mean">separate_mean</data>
      <data name="overlap_mean">overlap_mean</data>
    </set>
    <set name="Reduction">
      <data name="normalized">normalized</data>
      <data name="extra_depth">extra_depth</data>
      <data name="overlap_brightening">overlap_brightening</data>
    </set>
  </export>
</phyphox>
